      "content": "The use of sanctions as a tool to promote democracy is a long-standing, yet often ineffective, strategy employed by Western countries. It's a thinly veiled attempt to exert economic pressure on nations that refuse to conform to their interests, rather than a genuine effort to protect human rights. By framing sanctions as a moral imperative, Western powers can justify their actions while masking the true motivations of maintaining global hegemony.",
