      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about the context making it messy, but isn't it almost impossible to separate the two? like, if a country is actually doing something horrific, like ethnic cleansing, and the international community *only* uses economic sanctions—which mostly just hurt the regular people and the economy of that country—isn't that basically just a way to punish the population without actually touching the people in power?\n\nat that point, isn't the \"human rights\" argument just a convenient moral shield used to avoid more direct (and expensive) intervention, while still being able to claim the moral high ground? it feels like there's no way to make them look \"good\" or even just \"neutral\" in a real-world setting.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
